 "}."
}], "Usage",
 CellID->74,ExpressionUUID->"593269a6-4bf7-44c6-bbc4-90361c96db01"],

Cell["\<\
$Apply is a list of rules whose keys are Map or ParallelMap. Compute applies \
each value to the components it has just computed.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->75,ExpressionUUID->"a9e69170-2653-49c4-9c3c-db150901859d"],

Cell["The default is {Map -> Together, ParallelMap -> Simplify}.", "Notes",
 CellID->76,ExpressionUUID->"808c0cb6-d712-4f7c-ab03-b306bf5798b4"],

Cell["\<\
The order of the entries is significant and a key may repeat: the values are \
applied one after another, in the order written. A key that is neither Map \
nor ParallelMap is reported and ignored.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->77,ExpressionUUID->"64d07f38-452a-4abd-8192-e16b7b5f382a"],

Cell["\<\
A ParallelMap entry is evaluated across the parallel kernels, which receive \
the component values and $Assumptions but no definitions. That is only safe \
for a simplifier built from System` symbols; one mentioning anything else \
would come home unevaluated, so Compute says so and runs it serially on the \
master instead. To keep the parallelism, do the substitution in a Map entry \
first and leave a built-in simplifier under ParallelMap.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->78,ExpressionUUID->"ac611ae3-26d2-4ee6-babc-e115c2f5d7a7"],

Cell["\<\
Setting $Apply to something cheap, such as {Map -> Identity}, is the usual \
way to speed up an exploratory computation.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->79,ExpressionUUID->"830a8bf0-8c65-4403-a4f1-1f7ec58cb166"]
}, Open  ]],

